From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
Subject: econet-eth: DIAG log the eth-mangle actions and built L2 MACs

Live devmem dump of a committed BIND showed the dest MAC rewrite as
00:00:00:00:b6:41 - the top 4 bytes (the offset-0 eth mangle) are zero, so a
bound flow forwards to a bogus next hop. Log each eth mangle action
(offset/mask/val) and the assembled h_dest/h_source so the exact failing
write is visible on hardware before fixing the (endian-sensitive) mangle.
--- a/econet_ppe_offload.c
+++ b/econet_ppe_offload.c
@@ -208,6 +208,9 @@
 	void *dest = eth + act->mangle.offset;
 	const void *src = &act->mangle.val;
 
+	pr_info_ratelimited("econet-eth: ETHMANGLE off=%u mask=%08x val=%08x\n",
+			    act->mangle.offset, act->mangle.mask, act->mangle.val);
+
 	if (act->mangle.offset > 8)
 		return;
 
@@ -362,6 +365,9 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	pr_info_ratelimited("econet-eth: L2DIAG dst=%pM src=%pM\n",
+			    data.eth.h_dest, data.eth.h_source);
+
 	if (!is_valid_ether_addr(data.eth.h_source) ||
 	    !is_valid_ether_addr(data.eth.h_dest))
 		return -EINVAL;
